        "Florence breaks the script",
        "Lucy witnesses a man being killed in Florence, an event that abruptly interrupts the protected activity of sightseeing. George Emerson helps her, and the experience draws them into a conversation with an intimacy neither of them arranged. The incident has force because it puts beauty, danger, embarrassment, and compassion into the same afternoon. Lucy cannot return it neatly to the categories of approved experience through which her trip is supposed to proceed.\n\nOn a later country outing, George kisses Lucy. Charlotte intervenes, and Lucy leaves Florence under arrangements that treat the event as something best contained. Yet the departure leaves her without an honest language for the feelings the trip has raised. The social protection offered by the chaperone depends in part on silence. That silence creates a pattern Lucy will have to confront again when she returns to a setting where other people already imagine they know what her future should be."
